[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887828879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2887828879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2887828879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sIMWP","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T23:15:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T23:15:58Z","body":"To my knowledge XOR is a really bad obfuscation method, most hackers are very well aware of it and it's trivial to check for and reverse.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887828879/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887832036","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2887832036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2887832036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sINHk","user":{"login":"bearlikelion","id":3298808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTg4MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3298808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion","html_url":"https://github.com/bearlikelion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T23:19:24Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T23:19:24Z","body":"> To my knowledge XOR is a really bad obfuscation method, most hackers are very well aware of it and it's trivial to check for and reverse.\r\n\r\nWhile this is true, it's also computationally inexpensive. While _most hackers_ can still figure this out and dump the key, _most people_ would have a lot of trouble compared to just CTRL+F [this string](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.4.1-stable/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp#L298) in Ghidra which is the main problem I am looking to solve.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887832036/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":11,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887852866","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2887852866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2887852866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sISNC","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T23:46:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T23:46:47Z","body":"I commend the idea! You can never make something _completely_ secure anyway, especially using just client side methods, but every bit _more_ secure helps.\r\nI don't know what the \"industry standard\" technique for hiding your sensitive variables is. Perhaps someone more experienced can fill us in? But if other techniques are significantly more complex than the xor, I think this may be an acceptable quick improvement.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887852866/reactions","total_count":18,"+1":17,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887963138","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2887963138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2887963138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sItIC","user":{"login":"bearlikelion","id":3298808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTg4MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3298808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion","html_url":"https://github.com/bearlikelion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T02:05:44Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T02:05:44Z","body":"I attempted to try and pull the key using [gdke](https://github.com/char-ptr/gdke/tree/master) which just crashed during it's scan.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2887963138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888046397","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888046397","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888046397,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJBc9","user":{"login":"OmgItsBkid","id":8879659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzk2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8879659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid","html_url":"https://github.com/OmgItsBkid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmgItsBkid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T04:09:36Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T04:09:36Z","body":"> I attempted to try and pull the key using [gdke](https://github.com/char-ptr/gdke/tree/master) which just crashed during it's scan.\r\n\r\nThe problem is that sure, gdke will crash during its scan *now*, but in a single update it can account for this XOR and still be able to pull keys as easily as before. While it sounds like the idea is to stop the average person from being able to grab the key so easily, in reality the only people who have to care about a change like this are the makers of tools like gdke, and once they have, the average person is right back to grabbing keys again.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888046397/reactions","total_count":28,"+1":28,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888064400","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888064400","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888064400,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJF2Q","user":{"login":"bearlikelion","id":3298808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTg4MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3298808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion","html_url":"https://github.com/bearlikelion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T04:25:31Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T04:25:31Z","body":"> The problem is that sure, gdke will crash during its scan _now_, but in a single update it can account for this XOR and still be able to pull keys as easily as before. While it sounds like the idea is to stop the average person from being able to grab the key so easily, in reality the only people who have to care about a change like this are the makers of tools like gdke, and once they have, the average person is right back to grabbing keys again.\r\n\r\nCorrect, and completely understood. But as of now it's quite trivial to extract AES keys directly from a compiled binary. This provides a randomized user generated bitmask and the only way I could see it being found is through brute forcing every possible two byte hex value and trying to open the PCK. \r\n\r\nIt no longer is a click away and now is a tedious and potentially long process. \r\n\r\nMeasures like this _will always be_ a game of cat and mouse, but this at least provides some basic protection compared to essentially just leaving the key in plaintext.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888064400/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888092532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888092532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888092532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJMt0","user":{"login":"Jamsers","id":39361911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MzYxOTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39361911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers","html_url":"https://github.com/Jamsers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jamsers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T05:15:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T05:15:53Z","body":"> It no longer is a click away and now is a tedious and potentially long process.\r\n\r\nBut once gdke updates to account for this new obfuscation scheme (if this PR gets merged for example), then won't it go right back to being a click away?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888092532/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":9,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888098481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888098481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888098481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJOKx","user":{"login":"bearlikelion","id":3298808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTg4MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3298808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion","html_url":"https://github.com/bearlikelion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bearlikelion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T05:24:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T05:27:04Z","body":"> But once gdke updates to account for this new obfuscation scheme (if this PR gets merged for example), then won't it go right back to being a click away?\r\n\r\nThat's what I'm hoping to discuss with this PR, if you want _true security_ you should fork the engine and write custom encryption / ciphers yourself. But I see this as a better implementation than the current solution.\r\n\r\nThe reason I created the [example project](https://github.com/bearlikelion/godotxor) and provided the encryption key is to let people see if they're able to find it within the binaries themself. But I _think_ not knowing the key or bitmask used to cipher it will be somewhat difficult to solve.\r\n\r\nThere's _another problem_ of the key being left in memory, we could potentially unset the [key variable](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.4-stable/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp#L291) once the game initializes to avoid that, but I'm unsure if that may cause any other issues.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888098481/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":4,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888121253","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888121253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888121253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJTul","user":{"login":"fishhf","id":33946991,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTQ2OTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33946991?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf","html_url":"https://github.com/fishhf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fishhf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T06:05:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T06:05:51Z","body":"> > It no longer is a click away and now is a tedious and potentially long process.\r\n> \r\n> But once gdke updates to account for this new obfuscation scheme (if this PR gets merged for example), then won't it go right back to being a click away?\r\n\r\nThen the added code becomes irrelevant when it gets updated.\r\n\r\n> Right now, a big complaint I see online about Godot is it's security. After a hacker infected my game's leaderboards, I took some steps to rotate and secure my AES encryption key.\r\n\r\nBest to not trust the client, if that's not possible, can \"hide\" codes within the native side like godot extensions.\r\nOr instead of submiting scores to the leaderboard api directly, have the client submit the traces of game states, then the server side calculates the highscore with those traces.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888121253/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888134562","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888134562","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888134562,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJW-i","user":{"login":"takethebait","id":50055051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDU1MDUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50055051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait","html_url":"https://github.com/takethebait","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T06:27:45Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T06:27:45Z","body":"> if you want true security you should fork the engine and write custom encryption / ciphers yourself\r\n\r\nThis is probably the only reason why I would not want too many changes to this logic. Currently it is fairly trivial to modify the key logic (as shown by this PR). And I also think that, while I love open source, this is one thing where OSS is at a disadvantage. Modifying it here now will start an arms race. Don't get me wrong, I'm totally onboard with merging this because it's a fairly small change and compiling out the strings is also a good idea to me. But ultimately I would appreciate if this logic stays simple to replace.\r\n\r\nI would also argue that, if this PR would not be merged, the docs should get updated as they currently state:\r\n> Of course, the key needs to be stored in the binary, but if it's compiled, optimized and without symbols, it would take some effort to find it.\r\n\r\nwhich I believe has been proven to not really be true.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888134562/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":9,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888135866","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888135866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888135866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJXS6","user":{"login":"atzuk4451","id":20226261,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjI2MjYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20226261?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451","html_url":"https://github.com/atzuk4451","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atzuk4451/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T06:29:37Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T06:29:55Z","body":"@bearlikelion thank you for your effort. I was trying to figure out there can I set custom encryption for my export  and your code is great reference. Maybe if this is not merged it should be added to the docs so other people will have easier time making custom solutions.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888135866/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888189225","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888189225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888189225,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJkUp","user":{"login":"elenakrittik","id":77104725,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTA0NzI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77104725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik","html_url":"https://github.com/elenakrittik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elenakrittik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T07:41:44Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T07:48:29Z","body":"Like most encryption attempts, this one does not prevent malicious people from doing malicious things, and makes it unnecessarily hard for the faithful to do faithful things. Adding a function to get the \"true\" encryption key using a constant bitmask only adds an indirection layer that any \"hacker\" or reverse engineering tool will adapt to in no time: they'll just need to look for the bitmask constant via the newly-added function instead of looking for the key constant via the old decryption function.\n\nAs someone above have already said, this change will simply start an arms race between the RE tooling and Godot, wasting both sides' time in a hopeless attempt to prevent bad actors from exploiting game developers' (notice, not *engine* devs', *game* devs': any given exploit is a result of a *game's* flawed infrastructure, which the engine has no responsibility for or ability to affect) mistakes. This is evidenced by the decades of companies trying to add protection to their games and these protection systems all eventually getting destroyed by RE groups (or even removed by the companies themselves).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888189225/reactions","total_count":13,"+1":13,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888209314","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888209314","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888209314,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJpOi","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T08:03:12Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T08:03:12Z","body":"See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104719 by @bruvzg.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888209314/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888217893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888217893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888217893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJrUl","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T08:22:19Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T08:27:16Z","body":"> See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104719\r\n\r\nSingle byte XOR mask will slow down brute forcing the key from 30 sec to a few hours maximum, key derivation should make direct brute forcing pretty much impossible. But neither will do anything against manual hacking (require minimal reverse engineering skills, but should be considered trivial as well).\r\n\r\nEdit: But since there already are tools that are not brute forcing it but looking for decryption functions (essentially automating what you will do when looking for the key manually, https://github.com/char-ptr/godot-key-extract), both are completely useless (tool need updating to account for the change, but this is trivial to do).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888217893/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888259209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888259209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888259209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJ1aJ","user":{"login":"takethebait","id":50055051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDU1MDUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50055051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait","html_url":"https://github.com/takethebait","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T09:51:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T09:51:34Z","body":"The more I look at this the more I agree that this should not be merged and instead be clarified in the docs.\r\nThis is ultimately something that, if it is important to you as a developer, should be handled on a game-by-game basis or through the use of dedicated Anti-cheat / DRM software.\r\n\r\nI'd suggest to modify the documentation:\r\n- Stating that PCK encryption, while secure in theory, should not be considered safe since the key has to be embedded in the binary which can be easily found with bruteforce methods. It should not be used to hide or obscure things on the client and if you do networking, **NEVER EVER** trust anything the client sends to your server, always verify.\r\n- Maybe showcase how keystorage can be modified in the source code (you're compiling the templates yourself anyway so you should have the engine source code available) with the methods described in this PR and/or the one by @bruvzg (maybe as a sort of like a patchwork and a more involved solution).\r\n- Reiterate that this will not be enough to protect against malicous actors because again, you're shipping everything the client needs to decrypt your data to the client.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, it could also be mentioned that this is not a Godot issue or \"weakness\" since the other major engines are in the same position when it comes to protecting game files.\r\n\r\nI think that currently the docs convey a false sense of security to developers. \r\n\r\nAlso, if this is does get tackled in the core engine, there's probably going to be the same discussion again in a month or so.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888259209/reactions","total_count":24,"+1":24,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888293574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888293574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888293574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sJ9zG","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T10:54:49Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T12:03:27Z","body":"It looks like the discussion here revolves mainly around whether or not it's \"worth it\" to add _any_ security because it'll be broken anyway. \nThis is definitely an interesting discussion, but its one that would be best answered by a general policy around this question. I don't know if Godot has one already, but if it doesn't, maybe it's time to discuss it? In any case, i don't think this PR is the appropriate place to have this discussion.\n\nW.r.t the PR itself, if i understand correctly https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104719 is a \"more secure\" version of the same idea. So perhaps it would be better suited to address OP's concerns than the change proposed here.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888293574/reactions","total_count":13,"+1":13,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888361540","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2888361540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2888361540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sKOZE","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T12:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T12:30:23Z","body":"> Maybe showcase how keystorage can be modified in the source code (you're compiling the templates yourself anyway so you should have the engine source code available) with the methods described in this PR and/or the one by @bruvzg (maybe as a sort of like a patchwork and a more involved solution).\r\n\r\nWhen PCK encryption was introduced (if in favor of previous script encryption), there was an idea of allowing to use custom user-provided keyless white box decryption code, but it was too slow for any practical use (and all publicly available implementations have various security flaws as well).\r\n\r\nWith the key embedded in the executable, the security level will be always near-zero, and will remain the same no matter what you do. So only reasonable advice, assume PCK encryption is a “spoiler tag” preventing accidental reveal of the plain text from your project and nothing more.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888361540/reactions","total_count":17,"+1":17,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2890017620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-2890017620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":2890017620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sQitU","user":{"login":"DarioDaF","id":10617344,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjE3MzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10617344?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioDaF","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioDaF/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T08:00:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T08:00:51Z","body":"Any change that is merged in Godot will have no actual benefit for encryption (except annoy people who forked the engine to implement their security system) because reversing the system is trivial if all the games use the same scheme, is it hashing and deriving the key more, or xor or any other offline, no hardware check, I agree the security of the package should not be \"faked\", it's clearer to have it the way it is now","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2890017620/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3214064930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106512#issuecomment-3214064930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106512","id":3214064930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_kr0i","user":{"login":"tomsterBG","id":117642342,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwMUZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117642342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG","html_url":"https://github.com/tomsterBG","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-22T11:38:02Z","updated_at":"2025-08-22T11:39:51Z","body":"Sorry to bring up Roblox yet again, but when i was using it i noticed something interesting.\r\n\r\nThe client-server relationship is very powerful when all your variables are on the server and the client only stores the visual or front-end content. All the client should be able to do is send a request to the server for a level-up or upgrade, not do the upgrade itself. The server does the necessary checks to ensure that upgrades are processed appropriately. This also means if an upgrade costs money, the server must have the money and not request it from the client.\r\n\r\nHowever, having a server is not a luxury many devs can afford and especially no way if you want to have an offline playable game that still lets you use leaderboards and other server-related features.\r\n\r\nAll i'm trying to say here is that the solution for developers is in a correct client-server relationship and not in a better encryption on the client which given enough time will aways be available and broken through. This is what offline hacking means. Download some data and as long as you have yourself to worry about, you can spend as many hours as you want.\r\n\r\nIn fact i would go as far as to say, security per Godot game will be better if devs are incentivized to come up with their own systems because now hackers will have to RE every single game separately due to the differences in how things work, which takes more time and the developers actually learn how to defend their games.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, in Roblox the server automatically knows which client sent the request, preventing users from accessing the data of other users. If i was an admin and wanted admin-only functionality, nobody would be able to impersonate me because the server already knows who i am without me telling it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3214064930/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]